A||N||23||87GTBro||Who said Fieros DON'T catch on fire???||||1||
Z||000000||87GTBro||06-14-2001||03:07 PM||||I proved everybody wrong yesterday!!!  This could happen to any car, I know, but as I was driving to church 40 miles away, my right rear caliper froze.<P>After I got off the highway, I noticed that I had no more power when I pressed the gas pedal and that the car was slowing down really fast when I pressed in on the clutch.  It wasn't until I stopped at a traffic light and the man next to me honked and kindly told me that my car was on fire... that I knew what was wrong.<P>I quickly pulled into a McCoys Lumber yard parking lot and sure nuf!  My brake pads were burning right up!  I ran screaming and yelling looking for a water hose or something to put it out!  Fire and plastic cars don't mix!!!<P>A fork lift operator told me there was a hose out back so I ran faster than I ever had before...  I am so lucky there was a bucket right next to the hose.  After dousing the fire with two buckets of water... I could relax...<P>I couldn't drive the car anymore because the fire burnt through the brake line.  So I got a ride back home from my brother and borrowed a pickup and a flatbed trailer from my boss and went back to pick it up.  My poor baby is out of commision for now.<P>I only hope I didn't warp the rim when I doused it with water.  The entire rim was hot enough to sizzle the water, with both buckets full!<P>Word of advice...  CARRY A FIRE EXTINGUISHER IN YOUR CAR, JUST IN CASE!!!<P>We can't afford to lose anymore of these wonderful cars!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierochic88||06-14-2001||03:36 PM||||We once had a donor car that had it's entire side melted!  Apparently the gas line broke away and hit something and the entire driver's side caught on fire.  The guy had just rebuilt the engine and didn't connect it properly!  Yikes!<P>Jennifer<BR>Silver 88 GT<BR>Silver 86 Cp<BR>Cobalt Blue 85 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||06-14-2001||03:39 PM||||The first mod I do on any of my cars is to mount a fire extinguisher inside of it. Always better to have it and not need it. Also comes in handy durig road rage incidents...||||reg||1
