Z||000008||stsmithgt||06-14-2001||05:48 PM||||Let me get this straight...Your car is on fire, so you pull into a LUMBER yard, matchstick heaven!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/laugh2.gif">   <P>I suppose if anybody would have a fire exstinguisher, they would.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||84Bill||06-14-2001||05:53 PM||||LOL OMG!!! ROFLOL!!<BR>A double shot!!!<P>Good one stimpy and stsmithgt!||||reg||14
Z||000010||87GTBro||06-14-2001||06:00 PM||||I just pulled into the first available parking lot...  I was panicked looking for a water hose!!  I didn't even think about running inside to get an extinguisher...  <P>I was so freaked out that I forgot I had a gallon of H20 in the front compartment for emergencies!!! :-)<P>sqoach...  I wasn't working on it the day before... I think its just old.  I noticed a funny smell (like the brakes burning) on that same wheel a few days earlier, but I attributed it to hard driving.  The only thing I did before this happened was I washed the car.  That could have messed it up...<P>I have it all taken apart in the garage... I guess it's a good time to replace the axle seals as well!<P>I just have to wait for my parts to get here... :-(||||reg||1
Z||000011||stsmithgt||06-14-2001||07:03 PM||||It's fun to laugh at small problems(after the fact).  I had my car worked on by the dealership here and they left one of my sparkplug wires laying directly on the rear exhuast manifold, though they denied it completely.  I raced to worked not knowing this and picked up a miss pulling into the lot.  I popped the hood and saw two of my wires looking like a birthday candles with a 6" flame!¿? I made a wish and blew out the candles. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I almost didn't look until lunch time or when someone would have yelled "fire". Needless to say, but I will, I carry a fire extinguisher now.||||reg||1
Z||000012||grinthock||06-14-2001||08:13 PM||||I had an incident that ALMOST ended up in fire... I had just finished doing my custom intake project <BR> <A HREF="http://grinthock.2y.net/87intake.html" TARGET=_blank>http://grinthock.2y.net/87intake.html</A> <P>On my way home I smeeled somthing funny!  Opened the deck and all that fiber sh1t in the trunk was all smouldering smoking like a SOB... Funny part is i pulled into a GAS STATION (Not by the pumps!) to find out hte problem, the old lady that owned the place (it was in the boonies) told me to leave immediatly, before she called the cops!  I was like "Lady my car is gonna be on fire, just get me a damn cup of wateR!"<P>No damage done, thankfully, I pulled all that crap out the next day.  Some people need to realize that GAS DOESN'T BURN!!!  Fuel VAPOURS BURN!  Geez!  She was like "You are gonna make us all blow up!"  I lauged at her, kinda pissed her off more!||||reg||1
Z||000013||Cozmo||06-14-2001||09:43 PM||||<B>ROFLMFAO!!</B><P>Imagine what the people that worked there first thought...<P>"Apparently burning Fiero pulls into (lumber yard, gas station), frantic owner makes appeals for extinguishing materials"<P>Then, what they told their buddies over beers after work...<P>"No s**t! One of them Fi-aros comes screetchin' inta where I work today with fire and smoke jest pourin' out all over the place! Cheez, that crazy bastard 'bout run over (insert fellow co-worker here) and durn near crashed into the building! Lucky that thing didn't just go up in a big ball o' flames, bein' as they're totally made out of powdered magnesium and gunpowder. Some people got no sense, drivin' one a them firetraps.".<P>I keep a fire extinguisher in my car.  Scares the heck out of the passenger.<BR>I just say "Well, ya never know... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">..." <BR><B>C02M0</B> ||||reg||10
